+# Veterinarian Search Stays Out of Scope, Filtering by a Shown Attribute Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable records. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so whether it was deliberate stayed open.
+
+On 2026-11-05 the owner requested a filter on the veterinarian directory by specialty. That request touches NG-9. The owner decided the row at intake: "Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in."
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole and decline the filter.** Rejected by the owner's decision.
+2. **Remove NG-9.** Rejected: the owner kept free-text veterinarian search out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text search for a veterinarian stays declined. Narrowing the directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 is narrowed. Free-text search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian stays out of scope, and owners remain the only records searchable by text. Narrowing the veterinarian directory by an attribute the directory already shows is in scope. The first such capability is the specialty filter, `REQ-VET-003`.
+
+The filter is a URL contract only. No form, dropdown, or other page control comes with it; a visible control would be a separate request.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation as decided; the Non-Goals preamble names it.
+- A later request to filter by another shown attribute falls inside the narrowed row. A request for free-text veterinarian search still needs an owner decision at intake.
+- The rationale for declining free-text search stands: owner search already demonstrates paged prefix search once.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-9 row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the specialty filter the narrowing admits.
